From: Manu Goyal <manu.goyal2013@gmail.com>
Subject: Fix concurrent data races and segfaults during table resizing
References: https://github.com/efficient/libcuckoo/issues/174
Upstream: backported from commits 91b9c2d1, 59d72d74, and e355176a

Backports upstream fixes addressing data races and segfaults during table
resizing when concurrent reads and inserts take place (as tested in
universal_benchmark / read_insert_expansion). This introduces resize_counter_
synchronization, orders hashpower load after resize_counter, and synchronizes
access to all_locks_.

